WEBVTT

00:12.970 --> 00:18.710
Hikari ga sasu sora, umareochiru kage
In the bright sky illuminated by
sunlight, darkened shadows are born.

00:18.810 --> 00:24.150
Unmei wa dokomademo hikisakareru
Fate itself is being torn apart.

00:25.190 --> 00:30.150
Donna toki mo kesshite akiramenainara
If you never give up, no matter what happens,

00:30.330 --> 00:37.560
mada tozasareteru tobira kanarazu hiraku
Even that locked door will open for you.

00:38.530 --> 00:43.990
Eien datte dakishimete, fuuin mo tokihanachi
Embrace eternity and release the seal.

00:44.070 --> 00:49.940
Mamorubekimono ga ima kokoni wa arukara
Because the ones you wish
to protect are right here.

00:49.940 --> 00:55.880
Namida mo gyutto dakishimete,
yasashisa de tsutsumikomi
Embrace their tears with kindness.

00:55.880 --> 01:01.560
Nagareru mizu no youni tsuyoku nare
Become strong like the formless water,

01:01.560 --> 01:07.550
omouyouni tsuyoku nare
Become as strong as you wish to be.

01:07.700 --> 01:13.170
Mou jibun ni obienaide
Stop being afraid of yourself.

01:13.170 --> 01:19.800
Sou mirai wo osorenaide
Do not fear the future.

01:38.090 --> 01:39.420
What do you think?

01:46.200 --> 01:51.140
Our Fox Deity, Becomes a High School Student

01:52.670 --> 01:54.300
What am I supposed to think?

01:54.680 --> 01:57.300
You could have just worn regular clothes here.

01:57.810 --> 02:00.620
I thought you have to wear uniforms at school.

02:00.620 --> 02:05.450
Non-students are allowed in the Culture
Festival. You didn't need to wear a uniform.

02:08.020 --> 02:09.390
Akagi High School Culture Festival

02:09.390 --> 02:10.730
Akagi High School Culture Festival
Dad was whining about how he
wanted to come as we were leaving.

02:10.730 --> 02:14.560
Dad was whining about how he
wanted to come as we were leaving.

02:14.560 --> 02:18.430
Well, now. I need him to work
to put food on the table...

02:18.430 --> 02:24.070
But it does suck to have a job
that's the busiest on weekends.

02:24.340 --> 02:26.200
May I ask you something?

02:26.910 --> 02:29.440
What is Haruki-sama's occupation?

02:29.440 --> 02:31.440
Didn't I tell you before?

02:31.880 --> 02:34.470
He's a bus driver.

02:35.350 --> 02:38.680
I see. A bash driber.

02:38.890 --> 02:41.080
A "bus driver."

02:41.220 --> 02:43.320
Yes, I know. A bash driber.

02:44.260 --> 02:44.880
Ko...

02:45.030 --> 02:45.790
Yes.

02:46.330 --> 02:47.390
Bus...

02:47.860 --> 02:49.190
Bus...

02:49.600 --> 02:51.330
Driver.

02:51.670 --> 02:53.290
Driver...

02:53.570 --> 02:55.060
There, you said it.

02:55.170 --> 02:57.800
So yeah. He's a bus driver.

02:58.170 --> 03:00.730
Yes, a bash driber.

03:03.080 --> 03:07.020
Akagi High Culture Festival

03:07.020 --> 03:07.780
Akagi High Culture Festival
Toru.

03:07.780 --> 03:08.720
Akagi High Culture Festival
Yeah?

03:08.720 --> 03:08.920
Akagi High Culture Festival

03:08.920 --> 03:08.950
Akagi High Culture Festival
Take these coupons. I won't need them.

03:08.950 --> 03:11.180
Take these coupons. I won't need them.

03:11.720 --> 03:12.710
Thanks.

03:12.890 --> 03:14.320
I'll get going now.

03:14.320 --> 03:15.810
Just go and have some fun.

03:18.530 --> 03:20.860
Let's go together.

03:21.460 --> 03:24.490
I have to watch the shop...

03:24.570 --> 03:26.800
Let's go together.

03:26.800 --> 03:28.240
Later, okay?

03:28.240 --> 03:30.100
Let's go together.

03:30.100 --> 03:31.410
Look...

03:31.410 --> 03:33.430
Hey! Where's Toru and Ko?!

03:33.680 --> 03:34.940
You have to watch over them!

03:35.880 --> 03:40.370
They mentioned wanting to visit the
haunted house, so maybe they went there.

03:41.580 --> 03:44.950
I can tell exactly where Toru is.

03:44.950 --> 03:47.290
And the Mamorime will stay by his side.

03:47.490 --> 03:48.860
They'll be fine.

03:48.860 --> 03:51.550
Let's just go and enjoy a
date between grown-ups.

03:52.890 --> 03:55.260
You're worrying over nothing.

03:55.400 --> 03:57.160
I know... But still...

03:57.570 --> 04:01.600
Isn't the Culture Festival like a
party you hold within the school?

04:01.600 --> 04:02.840
Something like that.

04:02.840 --> 04:05.470
If it's a party, then we better enjoy it!

04:05.870 --> 04:08.770
I guess so.

04:09.010 --> 04:12.100
Oh? What's happening over there?

04:12.910 --> 04:15.150
It's something Class 2-3 is doing.

04:15.150 --> 04:16.640
It's called Balloon Art.

04:18.790 --> 04:20.190
Balloon Art?

04:20.960 --> 04:22.760
Your ears!

04:22.760 --> 04:23.890
Whoops. Sorry.

04:23.890 --> 04:25.620
You have to be more careful.

04:30.530 --> 04:33.360
What's this Balloon Art thing?

04:33.600 --> 04:39.810
It's when you twist and tie balloons to
make them look like dogs or rabbits...

04:39.810 --> 04:41.100
Actually, just look.

04:41.510 --> 04:43.810
I can't see.

04:50.290 --> 04:53.250
Let me ride on your shoulders!

04:53.450 --> 04:55.350
What?! No.

04:55.660 --> 04:56.660
Why?!

04:56.660 --> 04:57.920
Why?

04:59.930 --> 05:01.360
Because it's embarrassing...

05:01.500 --> 05:03.630
No, it's not.

05:03.630 --> 05:08.200
Maybe not for you, but it is for me.

05:08.200 --> 05:10.360
Oh, all right.

05:10.810 --> 05:17.730
In that case, I will have to forcefully
remove the dozens of people in front of me.

05:18.280 --> 05:22.740
You pitiful peasants. You have
no one to blame but Noboru.

05:25.350 --> 05:28.220
Please let me carry you...

05:29.320 --> 05:31.450
Here's a giraffe!

05:35.700 --> 05:36.960
Okay, go.

05:37.570 --> 05:38.530
There we go.

05:39.570 --> 05:40.260
S-She's light...

05:40.970 --> 05:43.460
I guess these yokai are all light.

05:43.970 --> 05:46.010
Wow! I can see it all!

05:46.010 --> 05:47.530
He's making something!

05:49.480 --> 05:51.150
- H-Hey! Stop moving around!
- What's that?!

05:51.150 --> 05:52.950
Come on, stand taller!

05:52.950 --> 05:54.380
Damn him... He's just showing off...

05:54.380 --> 05:56.940
Little bastard's trying to make us jealous!

05:58.520 --> 05:59.490
Takagami?

06:00.860 --> 06:03.190
H-Hey! Don't move!

06:03.660 --> 06:04.720
Sakura...

06:05.590 --> 06:07.560
What are you doing?

06:07.560 --> 06:09.500
Carrying her on my shoulders.

06:09.500 --> 06:11.470
Why?

06:11.470 --> 06:14.240
And in public, too! Without the slightest shame!

06:14.240 --> 06:17.500
In this situation, people will
yell at them to get a room!

06:17.970 --> 06:21.380
Wait, wouldn't that mean they're a couple?
Takagami and Tenko-san are...

06:21.380 --> 06:22.670
Noooooo!

06:23.540 --> 06:26.950
Hey, Sakura! How're you doing?

06:28.020 --> 06:29.920
Hello...

06:30.590 --> 06:31.780
Hello to you, too.

06:32.350 --> 06:34.220
What's your class doing?

06:37.530 --> 06:42.900
Um, we're running a café at
the Multimedia Classroom.

06:43.160 --> 06:45.830
Oh, really? I'll be sure to go there later.

06:46.430 --> 06:47.770
We'll welcome you...

06:47.870 --> 06:49.500
You're going, Noboru. Right?

06:49.700 --> 06:52.100
S-Sure.

06:53.880 --> 06:56.440
Is she trying show off how close they are to me?

06:56.440 --> 06:59.150
Is she trying to test my
feelings toward Takagami?

06:59.150 --> 07:00.640
I say, bring it on!

07:04.020 --> 07:05.380
I'll see you later then.

07:05.720 --> 07:06.690
Yeah...

07:18.200 --> 07:20.100
L-Let's go.

08:04.110 --> 08:05.240
The Sakasaen...

08:15.420 --> 08:16.490
What was that?!

08:16.490 --> 08:18.190
Somebody, call for a teacher!

08:18.190 --> 08:19.060
We have to evacuate everyone!

08:21.400 --> 08:22.360
Ko-chan...

08:27.600 --> 08:29.570
What was that?

08:34.080 --> 08:35.600
That surprised me.

08:36.040 --> 08:37.600
I hope it'll be okay...

08:41.850 --> 08:43.410
I'm thirsty...

08:43.750 --> 08:45.340
That is terrible to hear.

08:47.220 --> 08:50.350
Let's go drink something. I got
some free coupons from Noboru.

08:50.630 --> 08:52.790
We should find a place to rest.

08:56.160 --> 08:57.490
Thanks!

08:59.030 --> 09:00.230
Hey...

09:01.440 --> 09:04.340
Where did Ko-chan go?

09:05.840 --> 09:08.900
I'm sorry. I wasn't looking in front of me...

09:09.580 --> 09:10.870
Let me pay for that.

09:11.350 --> 09:16.910
It's okay. Don't worry about it.
I got it for free anyway.

09:17.020 --> 09:22.180
I can't do that. Please wait right here.

09:25.790 --> 09:29.250
Are they holding a church sale or something?

09:41.380 --> 09:42.340
Here you go.

09:44.850 --> 09:46.570
Thank you very much.

09:46.910 --> 09:48.810
Not at all.

09:49.580 --> 09:52.420
Are you interested in trees?

09:53.890 --> 09:55.910
You seemed to have been watching it intently.

09:56.590 --> 10:00.290
I was just wondering what kind of tree it is.

10:01.760 --> 10:04.860
My name is also based on a tree.

10:05.270 --> 10:07.290
Oh? So what's your name?

10:08.400 --> 10:09.300
Enju.

10:09.440 --> 10:11.960
There's a tree called Enju?

10:12.170 --> 10:14.870
Yes, I am Sister Enju.

10:15.280 --> 10:18.270
I work at the church near this school.

10:18.750 --> 10:21.650
If you would like,
please come visit on Sundays.

10:41.100 --> 10:42.130
Welcome.

10:43.440 --> 10:44.270
Thanks.

10:44.610 --> 10:47.100
Where's Tenko-san?

10:47.410 --> 10:55.040
We came in together, but she ran off,
mumbling about all the food looking good.

10:55.280 --> 10:57.520
- Meaning she just ditched me.
- Did she do it for me? No way...

10:57.520 --> 11:00.420
- I have no idea where she went.
- Did she do it for me? No way...

11:00.960 --> 11:05.290
Even if that's the case, does it mean
she noticed my feelings for Takagami?

11:05.290 --> 11:09.460
Did she give me some time alone
with him because she supports me?

11:09.460 --> 11:14.940
But that means, at the very least,
Tenko-san isn't Takagami's girlfriend...

11:14.940 --> 11:19.570
Then again, the next person I
have to worry about is Ko-chan...

11:19.570 --> 11:22.280
I still don't know what her
relationship with Takagami is.

11:22.280 --> 11:24.610
I want to know... I want to ask...

11:25.080 --> 11:25.880
Sakura?

11:26.710 --> 11:29.010
Oh, I'm sorry. So what will you have?

11:31.350 --> 11:35.020
I'll have the Scone Combo, please.

11:35.190 --> 11:37.490
Sure thing.

11:44.330 --> 11:46.270
My shift is over.

11:46.630 --> 11:48.120
Do you mind if I sit here?

11:48.400 --> 11:50.460
Go right ahead.

11:55.210 --> 11:58.550
I have to ask him what his
relationship with Ko-chan is.

11:58.550 --> 12:02.880
I'm prepared for any answer I get...

12:09.160 --> 12:12.730
No I'm not! How can I be prepared for this?!

12:12.730 --> 12:15.320
I can't do it. But I still want to know!

12:15.830 --> 12:18.700
Why isn't Sakura-san saying anything?

12:19.130 --> 12:22.400
Is she mad or something? I can't really tell.

12:22.870 --> 12:25.740
But I should do something...

12:26.670 --> 12:27.570
I know...

12:28.140 --> 12:31.980
Teraoka and some friends
from his class formed a band.

12:31.980 --> 12:33.710
They're going to have a concert today.

12:35.080 --> 12:37.550
You're done with your shift, right?
Do you want to go together?

12:37.750 --> 12:41.020
So it'll be you, me, and who else?

12:41.690 --> 12:45.890
I was planning on just you and me going...

12:46.060 --> 12:47.120
For now, at least.

12:48.000 --> 12:49.590
You don't want to?

12:52.830 --> 12:54.320
I do want to.

12:54.500 --> 12:56.700
Then let's go after I finish this.

12:56.700 --> 12:57.470
Sure!

13:02.680 --> 13:04.580
Toru! Toru!

13:05.180 --> 13:07.170
Here! Eat anything you want!

13:07.410 --> 13:10.010
Wow, where'd you get all these?

13:10.450 --> 13:12.250
They all gave them to me!

13:12.750 --> 13:15.550
Did you use some kind of spell again?

13:15.690 --> 13:18.490
Come on, is that how you see me?

13:20.900 --> 13:26.890
All I did was stare at what they were
selling and said, "This looks so good!"

13:27.270 --> 13:30.730
They're the ones who said,
"G-G-Go right ahead and take it."

13:30.910 --> 13:32.940
And they handed them to me.

13:32.940 --> 13:35.910
I never once said I wanted
to eat them or anything!

13:37.680 --> 13:42.010
I'll admit I only went after the ones
with boys watching the stalls...

13:45.290 --> 13:46.010
Oh...

13:46.250 --> 13:50.360
Next, I'll turn into a man and
go after the stalls with girls.

13:50.360 --> 13:51.260
Stop it.

13:51.930 --> 13:53.590
I'm joking. Here!

13:53.930 --> 13:55.620
Oh, geez...

13:55.930 --> 13:58.730
But you have it already, so I might as well.

13:59.170 --> 14:01.070
I'll take the okonomiyaki.

14:01.500 --> 14:02.940
Which one do you want, Ko-chan?

14:05.770 --> 14:07.330
I will have the noodles, please.

14:08.280 --> 14:09.830
Let's eat!

14:10.380 --> 14:11.310
Yes, let us eat.

14:12.210 --> 14:13.940
By the way, where's Noboru?

14:14.820 --> 14:17.350
Who knows?

14:17.350 --> 14:18.180
What's that supposed to mean?

14:18.290 --> 14:21.650
Life is all about facing challenges. That's what.

14:32.570 --> 14:33.190
Hey...

14:38.770 --> 14:42.260
Other people can't see those ears...

14:43.140 --> 14:44.040
Ku-cha...

14:55.060 --> 14:58.250
Hey. It's been a while, Kugen.

14:58.790 --> 15:00.090
What a coincidence.

15:00.430 --> 15:02.760
What's with that outfit?

15:03.000 --> 15:04.790
It's this school's uniform.

15:05.470 --> 15:07.730
Is there a reason for you to wear it?

15:08.140 --> 15:09.190
Is there one not to?

15:09.740 --> 15:11.230
Well, whatever.

15:11.670 --> 15:15.840
Anyway, word of you getting
freed was true after all.

15:16.740 --> 15:18.440
How many decades has it been?

15:18.610 --> 15:20.310
Decades?

15:20.310 --> 15:22.870
Don't you mean centuries?

15:23.920 --> 15:24.980
You haven't changed.

15:25.490 --> 15:26.750
That's not entirely true.

15:29.820 --> 15:31.690
You're the one who hasn't changed.

15:32.790 --> 15:36.460
He's Gyokuyo. A tenko, just like me.

15:37.560 --> 15:42.330
So that means Gyokuyo-san is also a fox, right?

15:42.800 --> 15:44.100
A silver fox, if you will.

15:44.410 --> 15:47.000
Oh, a silver fox.

15:48.040 --> 15:48.770
Are you two friends?

15:49.110 --> 15:51.100
What?! Friends?!

15:51.350 --> 15:52.780
No way!

15:53.710 --> 15:54.810
Oh...

15:55.750 --> 15:59.410
So Gyokuyo-san, how do you
write your name out in characters?

15:59.750 --> 16:01.410
The "Gyoku" part is the same "tama" as jade.

16:01.720 --> 16:06.630
For the second half, you first write out the
character for light, then two "yo" next to it.

16:06.630 --> 16:09.290
You then write the top half
of the character for "gather."

16:11.500 --> 16:13.690
How about I keep it simple
and just call you Tama-chan?

16:14.800 --> 16:15.530
Ta?!

16:15.670 --> 16:17.190
That sounds great!

16:18.910 --> 16:20.000
Tama-chan!

16:22.580 --> 16:24.540
I don't like that name...

16:25.150 --> 16:30.910
I think it's perfect, Ta-Ta-Tama-chan!

16:32.690 --> 16:37.090
Mamorime! Since he's here
anyway, give Tama taiyaki!

16:37.320 --> 16:38.090
Sure.

16:38.830 --> 16:39.950
Here you go, Tama-san.

16:41.060 --> 16:41.990
Tama-san!

16:43.630 --> 16:44.430
Thank you...

16:49.540 --> 16:52.990
The oni have been up to something recently.

16:54.480 --> 16:56.570
Expensive yokai-related artifacts...

16:57.510 --> 17:01.880
...were stolen from the homes
of collectors all around Honshu.

17:01.880 --> 17:05.280
They're then resold at exorbitant
prices on the black market.

17:06.420 --> 17:10.410
Though they've done this for
as long as I can remember...

17:10.860 --> 17:13.020
...they've become much more
conspicuous over the past few months.

17:13.590 --> 17:19.120
Some say they have gained so much money,
there is nothing they can't buy.

17:20.300 --> 17:22.390
What are they collecting so much money for?

17:22.970 --> 17:26.870
Who knows? But that makes it
all the more suspicious.

17:27.210 --> 17:30.800
A group of oni gathering dirty money...

17:31.450 --> 17:33.500
It's so fitting.

17:33.810 --> 17:37.110
You know how the human's folk tales
always have oni hoarding treasure.

17:37.620 --> 17:38.980
This may be serious...

17:39.750 --> 17:44.750
I hear that group of oni currently
reside somewhere around here.

17:46.390 --> 17:47.790
Hey!

17:48.060 --> 17:49.050
My balloon...

17:49.860 --> 17:52.590
Doesn't this interest you?

17:53.430 --> 17:55.870
Why they're gathering so much money...

17:56.740 --> 17:58.640
What they're trying to do...

17:58.810 --> 18:01.710
And the money itself.

18:03.080 --> 18:03.810
How about it?

18:05.710 --> 18:06.770
How about what?

18:07.380 --> 18:08.410
We'll split it both ways.

18:15.660 --> 18:16.450
I'll pass.

18:16.860 --> 18:17.650
Why?

18:17.990 --> 18:19.930
I have my own job to do.

18:20.130 --> 18:20.920
What job?

18:21.700 --> 18:23.130
Babysitting this one over here.

18:24.900 --> 18:29.430
I can't tell whether you're being serious or not...

18:29.740 --> 18:31.360
I'm serious.

18:43.880 --> 18:45.250
I take back what I said earlier.

18:45.650 --> 18:47.020
You've changed...

18:47.720 --> 18:48.860
Thank you for the food.

18:48.860 --> 18:50.690
Not at all.

18:57.060 --> 18:59.060
He's leaving...

19:00.470 --> 19:03.370
Did you just have a fight?

19:04.810 --> 19:07.800
It's always been like this between us.

19:08.280 --> 19:11.840
We'll get together if we want.
We don't if we don't want to.

19:12.380 --> 19:16.250
It's much easier that way,
and it makes the relationship last longer, too.

19:20.190 --> 19:21.590
Thank you for the food.

19:22.660 --> 19:25.930
Thank you! Thank you, baby!

19:25.930 --> 19:27.020
Thank you very much!

19:31.700 --> 19:33.330
Thanks!

19:35.540 --> 19:38.510
Looks like the audience liked their
act more than their singing...

19:38.510 --> 19:39.270
Yup.

19:39.740 --> 19:41.210
Do you want to go now?

19:41.780 --> 19:42.330
Sure.

19:44.010 --> 19:45.280
Oh, yeah.

19:45.280 --> 19:47.470
Do you want to try some of the
chicken skewers our class is making?

19:50.380 --> 19:51.720
Miyabe-san...

19:51.890 --> 19:54.880
Thank you for coming!

19:55.020 --> 19:58.010
Momiji-chan!

19:58.190 --> 20:01.860
I don't remember Miyabe-san
being such a bubbly person.

20:07.970 --> 20:12.770
When my heart beats for you,

20:13.840 --> 20:18.800
I just know you can hear it.

20:19.550 --> 20:24.480
I hate being alone.

20:25.050 --> 20:31.920
As my emotions keep wavering,
take me along for the ride. I want you.

20:34.560 --> 20:38.220
Each day happens so fast.

20:40.330 --> 20:44.200
But among everything,

20:44.910 --> 20:45.010
If there is something that never changes,
tell me what it is.

20:45.010 --> 20:46.340
If there is something that never changes,
tell me what it is.
Takagami!

20:46.340 --> 20:48.310
If there is something that never changes,
tell me what it is.
- Hey! Ow...
- The chicken skewers!

20:48.310 --> 20:49.140
If there is something that never changes,
tell me what it is.
- Let's go!

20:49.140 --> 20:50.310
If there is something that never changes,
tell me what it is.
- H-Hey, Sakura!
- Let's go!

20:50.310 --> 20:51.210
If there is something that never changes,
tell me what it is.

20:51.210 --> 20:56.440
It will wipe those tears away.

20:57.650 --> 21:05.580
The processes of smiles, courage and love,

21:06.690 --> 21:09.090
Those can't be found alone.

21:09.360 --> 21:14.100
Your kindness and warmth can make me change.

21:14.100 --> 21:17.240
Your kindness and warmth can make me change.
What's with those glances?

21:17.670 --> 21:18.310
Is that supposed to be a challenge against me?!

21:18.310 --> 21:21.440
Now I can smile to blow it all away!
Is that supposed to be a challenge against me?!

21:21.440 --> 21:24.740
Now I can smile to blow it all away!

21:35.390 --> 21:41.850
Sora no hate ga tsunagaru basho wo
Where the horizon meets the earth,

21:42.330 --> 21:49.570
no ni saku hana wa mada kitto shiranai
The flower growing in the wild remains unaware.

21:50.900 --> 21:57.400
Kokoyori ii sekai ga aruto
While thinking that there
is a world better than this.

21:57.540 --> 22:05.180
Kokoro wa itsumo hane wo hirogetagaru
They always desire to spread
the wings of their hearts.

22:06.090 --> 22:13.120
Yume dakede owarasenai
Don't let it end as just a dream,

22:13.730 --> 22:20.220
chansu ga aru hazusa
There's always a chance.

22:20.430 --> 22:27.870
Daijoubu bokura ha hitori janai
It's all right. We are not alone.

22:27.870 --> 22:35.520
Kaze ga nanika wo iouto shiteru
The winds are telling us something.

22:35.520 --> 22:43.160
Daijoubu kanarazu umaku yareru
It's all right. You can do it.

22:43.160 --> 22:54.400
Omoi wa itsuka jibun wo kaeru michi ni naru
Those dreams are a path you'll change yourself.

23:05.280 --> 23:06.710
I am here.

23:07.710 --> 23:09.080
How are you?

23:11.020 --> 23:12.110
Did you see it?

23:12.290 --> 23:15.150
Yes. There is no need to worry.

23:16.260 --> 23:18.550
Then it is time...

23:19.530 --> 23:22.520
Yes... It is...

23:24.970 --> 23:25.930
Next Time

23:25.930 --> 23:27.430
Next Time
Home shopping can be really convenient.

23:27.430 --> 23:29.840
Next Time
But you always end up
buying stuff you don't need.

23:29.840 --> 23:32.210
Next Time
And you might even forget that
you actually bought it before.

23:32.210 --> 23:34.440
Next Time
Hey, I didn't order this!

23:34.440 --> 23:34.670
Next Time

23:34.670 --> 23:35.140
Next Time
Next time, "Our Fox Deity, Makes a Call."

23:35.140 --> 23:36.780
Next Time
Our Fox Deity, Makes a Call
Next time, "Our Fox Deity, Makes a Call."

23:36.780 --> 23:36.910
Next Time
